.git
.github
docs
vagrant
*.code-workspace
spoutbreeze-web/tmp
spoutbreeze-web/logs
spoutbreeze-web/data
**/build
**/.gradle
app/tmp
app/logs

# Environment configuration is supplied at runtime, never baked in. The
# customer builds their own app/config/config-production.ini from the
# tracked .sample; if one exists on the build host it must not reach the
# image, because it can carry spoutbreeze.secret_key — the key that
# decrypts every stored destination credential.
app/config/config-production.ini
app/config/config-staging.ini
app/config/config-local.ini

# The development and test files carry working credentials. Development
# mounts app/ from the working tree, so they are never needed inside an
# image — and an image that ships them hands a customer our dev API key
# and destination encryption key.
app/config/config-development.ini
app/config/config-test.ini
deploy/.env
deploy/.env.*

# The image takes its vendor from dist/vendor (dev-free, symlinks
# dereferenced by tools/sb); the working-tree vendor carries dev
# dependencies and framework symlinks, and is for local development only.
vendor

